From: openEuler RISC-V Maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] tests: select the Python 3.11 context protocol exception

Python 3.11 changed with-statement missing-context-protocol errors to TypeError
(bpo-12022). Keep both malformed-manager tests, the old-version AttributeError
assertion, and the exact CPython 3.11 error/message assertion for new versions.
No library implementation, discovered test, default command or waiver changes.

References:
https://docs.python.org/3.11/whatsnew/3.11.html#other-language-changes
https://github.com/python/cpython/blob/v3.11.6/Lib/test/test_contextlib.py
https://github.com/python/cpython/blob/v3.10.14/Lib/test/test_contextlib.py

--- a/test/test_contextlib.py
+++ b/test/test_contextlib.py
@@ -497,3 +497,7 @@ class TestContextDecorator(unittest.TestCase):
-        with self.assertRaises(AttributeError):
+        if sys.version_info >= (3, 11):
+            assertion = self.assertRaisesRegex(TypeError, 'the context manager')
+        else:
+            assertion = self.assertRaises(AttributeError)
+        with assertion:
             with mycontext():
                 pass
@@ -509,3 +513,8 @@ class TestContextDecorator(unittest.TestCase):
-        with self.assertRaises(AttributeError):
+        if sys.version_info >= (3, 11):
+            assertion = self.assertRaisesRegex(
+                TypeError, 'the context manager.*__exit__')
+        else:
+            assertion = self.assertRaises(AttributeError)
+        with assertion:
             with mycontext():
                 pass
